    "q-181353": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181353",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the solution to the inequality $\\frac{5t-6}{2}\\le 1.$\n\nThe solution is $t$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5t-6}{2}\\le 1 \\\\ 2\\cdot (\\frac{5t-6}{2}) & \\le 2\\cdot 1 \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot (\\frac{5t-6}{\\cancel{2}}) & \\le 2 \\\\ 5t-6 & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5t-6 & \\le 2 \\\\ 5t-6+6 & \\le 2+6 \\\\ 5t & \\le 8 \\\\ \\frac{5t}{5} & \\le \\frac{8}{5} \\\\ t & \\le \\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t\\le \\frac{8}{5}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
